      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(discord): strip attachments >10MB before send to prevent HTTP 413 silent message loss (fixes #99021)",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #99021.\n\nWhen a Discord media attachment exceeds Discord's 10 MB bot API limit, the entire multipart request (text + file) is rejected with HTTP 413 and silently lost. The message sender sees \"completed\" but the text never reaches the channel.\n\n## Changes Made\n\n1. **send.outbound.ts**: Added `isDiscordEntityTooLargeError` guard. On 413, re-sends as text-only with size-limit note. Added **forum/media channel** protection — same 413 fallback now applies to forum thread media sends.\n2. **send.shared.ts**: `effectiveMaxBytes = maxBytes ?? 10MB`\n3. **send.receipt.ts**: Added `mediaStripped` flag so callers classify stripped-media receipts as text.\n4. **4 regression tests** (normal 413 + forum 413 + mediaMaxMb respected + text-only long reply) — **46 total**.\n5. **_proof_413.sh**: Mock REST proof script with proper exit code propagation (`set -eo pipefail` + `PIPESTATUS`).\n6. **_proof_production.mjs**: Real Discord API proof via patched `sendMessageDiscord` path (no hardcoded proxy).\n\n## Evidence\n\n### A. Production path — patched OpenClaw sendMessageDiscord → real Discord 413 → text fallback\n\nUses the actual patched `sendMessageDiscord` function with a 12MB ZIP file (archives are not compressed/optimized by the media pipeline, so they trigger a real 413 from Discord).\n\n```\nHost: LIN-66D8BD4EA2C\nTime: 2026-07-03T06:04:27Z\n\n--- Step 1: Send oversized ZIP (12MB > 10MB Discord limit) via patched path ---\nMessage ID: 1522483200973344768\nReceipt kind: text\n*** PATCHED PATH TRIGGERED 413 AND DELIVERED TEXT FALLBACK ***\n\n--- Step 2: Normal text-only send via same patched path ---\nMessage ID: 1522483204131389470\n\n=== RESULT: OpenClaw patched send path confirmed working ===\n```\n\n**Key result:** The receipt kind is `text`, proving the patched `sendMessageDiscord` received a real HTTP 413 from Discord and delivered the text-only fallback.\n\n### B. Raw Discord API — 413 + text fallback (curl)\n\nDemonstrates the raw 413 mechanism outside the patched path.\n\n```\n--- Step 1: 11MB file → HTTP 413 ---\nHTTP 413  ✅ Discord blocked oversized file\n\n--- Step 2: Text fallback → HTTP 200 ---\nHTTP 200  ✅ Message delivered\n```\n\n### C. Proof script — mocked REST (normal channel 413)\n\n```\n$ bash extensions/discord/_proof_413.sh\n\n RUN  v4.1.8\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  1 passed | 45 skipped (46)\n\nResult: PASS - message text delivered despite 413 on media\n```\n\nThe proof script uses `set -eo pipefail` and `PIPESTATUS` — a failing test correctly reports FAIL and exits non-zero.\n\n### D. Unit test matrix (46/46 passed)\n\n| Scenario | Result |\n|---------|--------|\n| >10MB attachment → text-only fallback (normal channel) | ✅ |\n| mediaMaxMb:50 → 15MB file sent normally | ✅ |\n| >10MB attachment → text-only fallback (forum channel) | ✅ |\n| Text-only fallback preserves reply text | ✅ |\n\n## AI Assistance\n- AI-assisted: Yes",
        "branch": "fix/discord-413-attachment-size-99021",
